---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import NextProject from "../../components/NextProject.astro";
import { laundryStatus } from "../../data/projects";
import { laundryDates } from "../../data/experience";
---

<Base
  title="UVM LaundryLink — Ivan Minier"
  theme="campus"
  image="/media/og/laundrylink.png"
  description="An independent student prototype for campus laundry. Currently temporarily unavailable while its server is offline."
>
  <section class="campus-opening wrap-wide">
    <img
      class="campus-logo"
      src="/media/laundrylink/logo.webp"
      width="512"
      height="512"
      alt="LaundryLink identity mark"
    />
    <p class="eyebrow">A student project / {laundryDates}</p>
    <h1>UVM LaundryLink</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A small campus problem:
      <br />
      is it worth walking to the laundry room?
    </p>
    <p class="role-line">
      Creator · Product, interface & AI-assisted front-end development
    </p>
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>{laundryStatus.label}.</strong> {laundryStatus.notice}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap-wide campus-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The everyday problem</p>
      <h2>
        A wasted trip
        <br />
        is still a wasted trip.
      </h2>
      <p>
        The prototype brought room discovery and machine status into a
        phone-friendly page, so a student could decide where to go before
        leaving their room.
      </p>
      <p>
        I worked on the product structure and interface with AI-assisted coding.
        The useful lesson was practical: a clear interface still depends on the
        availability of its data source.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Implemented prototype features</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Find a room</h3>
          <p>
            Campus room discovery, search, and machine availability when the
            data source was available.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Keep it close</h3>
          <p>Saved favorites and dark mode for repeat visits.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Set an alert</h3>
          <p>
            SMS notifications as part of the historical prototype. Live
            availability and alerts cannot be demonstrated during the outage.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap-wide case-ending">
    <div>
      <h2>A prototype with a real dependency.</h2>
      <p>
        The domain remains active. Live rooms and alerts depend on the server
        and are unavailable during the outage. LaundryLink is independent and is
        not an official UVM product.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://uvmlaundry.com">
        Project domain ↗
      </a>
    </div>
    <NextProject slug="uvm-laundrylink" />
  </section>
</Base>
